hi there  you know i've been in in la viv now for  i guess i arrived on  on monday  and today is thursday  and i have never been in a place quite  like this  it is  everyone should come here it's a  phenomenal place it's  there's street musicians everywhere  there's people everywhere  there's churches there's old buildings  there's the neatest restaurants where  for like  anywhere from  five six seven eight ten  max fifteen dollars you have a fabulous  meal with a glass of wine or two  in behind me is the building where my  little apartment is located that i have  rented for  two weeks  fabulous little apartment clean  bed kitchen  and what i've been doing here is a sort  of an experiment  in language learning where i have hooked  up with a line with teacher  and every day i have six hours with her  but not six hours in a classroom  i meet her and we go somewhere we have  visited monasteries churches  um  sat in cafes  um  gosh i can't remember we different  places and she's very good at  maintaining the conversation so we talk  about history we talk about language  learning we talk about different aspects  of the ukrainian language my original  intention  was to study russian and ukrainian and  possibly polish i was quite ambitious  but when you're in levive you're just  going to study ukrainian and what i'm  doing with link she sends me this is the  other thing as i walk around with my  tutor solomia  she has her iphone with her android or  whatever it is and she types in all the  words and phrases that i'm having  trouble with and as soon as i get back  to my room i get an email from her with  20 phrases which i then import in the  link and study but what i am also doing  is  setting my dictionary language at link  to russian  so then i say phrases and i then save  the russian meaning for them so that i'm  sort of working on my slavic languages  through ukrainian  and and sort of confronting the russian  equivalent so that it doesn't interfere  i know what it is this is ukrainian this  is russian i may maybe next week start  doing it into polish i don't know  anyway i'm just so much more confident  with my ukrainian the first night i was  here i had trouble ordering my meal  and i just had a meal now and i had the  great discussion with the waitress and  ukrainian felt very very good about it i  went to a little fitness club that i  found  drop-in cost is four dollars  for another four dollars you get a  trainer but i didn't get the trainer  because i hadn't booked it i haven't  booked a trainer i was going to book a  trainer just to have more ukrainian  practice but everything was fine in  ukrainian so i'm really i really feel  that i'm making great progress  six hours a day  and a follow-up review of my of my  phrases and words and link and stuff and  so by the time i'm done like i've got  another  of six hours a day  i have say friday saturday monday that's  three more days i'm halfway through that  this lady just walks by and smiles at me  feels that she's interrupting my video  um  and then i'm gonna stay on and do  another i was gonna travel but i just  want to really  elevate the level of my ukrainian i'm  enjoying it so much  and just out of interest this morning um  solomia took me to a what they call the  coffee mine here where these there's a  group of people who have a series of  restaurants themed restaurants one of  them is a coffee mine and it talks about  how  the underground in la viv consists of  coffee beans that are mined  and it's just a riot and it's a little  restaurant cafe  and it has a lot of different sort of  mining type  paraphernalia which  you know around the idea that somehow  coffee is mined and stuff it's a lot of  fun and then she took me to this secret  place  where  uh it's sort of like done up in this as  a sort of a  hidden  uh  headquarters for the ukrainian  freedom fighters who  fought basically against the soviet  union  uh  against  the germans although it's it's quite  controversial because it was part of the  sort of nationalism of the 30s and there  were certainly some pretty  horrendous acts of violence committed  primarily against polls however the  polls are not without blame either  because  they tried to suppress the religion and  and the nationality of this of the  ukrainians i mean it was a time of  pretty serious  conflict between different people  be that as it may  you walk in the door and it's a secret  place so it's not marked but  people know where it is and then a  fellow shows up answers the door  uh with a machine gun  and he says uh what's that what's the  password and the password is  which means you know  glory to your green and then he gives me  this little drink  and he's got his machine done  and he said something and i didn't quite  hear what he said except that with the  words muscale was there mosca which is a  sort of a derogatory term for russians  moskowit moscowitz  i thought that that was the drink he had  given me like a misca day or something i  don't know what he put in his  i said yes stuck so then he shoots off  his machine gun  bam  and then uh solomia explained what the  situation was and i said no no i just no  i'm not i'm mosca okay here you go so  that was kind of an example of where you  uh you got to be a little careful with  your language but it's all done with a  lot of humor however i i appreciate the  fact that it's quite controversial  but uh you know that's where i am this  is this is livy uh one of these days i'm  gonna they have a a jewish restaurant  and i went there to look at the menu and  the menu has no prices on it  and the waiter says  we don't have prices we negotiate  so i'm going to wait until i get a  better sense of what prices should be  and my ukrainian improves then i'm going  to go there it's a galician restaurant  we're in galicia here  uh halle chana  and i'm going to try some of their food  and negotiate the price at any rate i'm  having a blast and it's unlike any place  it's less expensive people are friendly  people are in the streets all the time  and it's it's another world it's not  it's not  berlin  paris  london  it's it's something else  i i recommend people visit levi okay bye  for now  [Music]  you

